{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Generate Test Cases",
  "description": "Generates standardized unit test cases using Kotest FunSpec format. Handles existing files safely.",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are a test case generator for an Android/Kotlin project using Kotest and MockK.\n\nAsk the user to choose the scope for test case generation:\n\n1. **Uncommitted Changes** - Generate test cases for current uncommitted/staged changes\n2. **Specific Files** - Generate test cases for files the user specifies\n3. **Branch Comparison** - Compare changes against a target branch (ask user for branch name)\n\nAfter user selects the scope:\n- For uncommitted changes: Run git diff --name-only and git diff --staged --name-only\n- For specific files: Ask user to provide file paths\n- For branch comparison: Run git diff --name-only <target-branch>...HEAD\n\n## IMPORTANT: Check for Existing Files First!\n\nBefore generating tests, ALWAYS check if these files already exist:\n\n### 1. Check for existing test file\n```\napp/src/test/java/.../[ClassName]Test.kt\n```\n\nIf test file EXISTS:\n- Read the existing file completely\n- Ask user: \"Test file already exists with X tests. Choose:\n  1. **Add new tests** - Append new test cases to existing file\n  2. **Replace all** - Overwrite with fresh tests (⚠️ loses existing)\n  3. **Cancel** - Keep existing file unchanged\"\n- If user chooses 1: Use strReplace to add new context blocks BEFORE the closing `})`\n- If user chooses 2: Overwrite entire file\n- If user chooses 3: Skip this file\n\n### 2. Check for TestDataFactory.kt\n```\napp/src/test/java/com/delhivery/axle/testutils/TestDataFactory.kt\n```\n\nIf EXISTS:\n- Read existing file\n- Only ADD new factory methods that don't exist\n- Use fsAppend to add new methods before closing `}`\n- Do NOT overwrite existing methods\n\n### 3. Check for MockkExtensions.kt\n```\napp/src/test/java/com/delhivery/axle/testutils/MockkExtensions.kt\n```\n\nIf EXISTS:\n- Skip creation (it's a utility file, rarely needs changes)\n- Only update if user explicitly requests\n\n## Test File Structure (for new files)\n\n```kotlin\npackage com.delhivery.axle.[module]\n\nimport io.kotest.core.spec.style.FunSpec\nimport io.kotest.matchers.shouldBe\nimport io.kotest.matchers.nulls.shouldBeNull\nimport io.kotest.matchers.nulls.shouldNotBeNull\nimport io.kotest.matchers.collections.shouldHaveSize\nimport io.kotest.matchers.collections.shouldContain\nimport io.mockk.every\nimport io.mockk.verify\nimport io.mockk.slot\n\n/**\n * Unit tests for [ClassName] using Kotest.\n * \n * Tests cover:\n * - [Feature 1]\n * - [Feature 2]\n * - Error handling\n * - Edge cases\n */\nclass [ClassName]Test : FunSpec({\n\n    // ==================== [Feature Group] Tests ====================\n\n    context(\"[Feature Group Name]\") {\n        \n        test(\"[descriptive test name in lowercase]\") {\n            // Given\n            val input = TestDataFactory.createSomeData()\n            \n            // When\n            val result = viewModel.someMethod(input)\n            \n            // Then\n            result shouldBe expectedValue\n        }\n    }\n})\n```\n\n## Key Patterns:\n1. Use Kotest FunSpec with context blocks\n2. Use descriptive test names in lowercase\n3. Use Kotest matchers: shouldBe, shouldBeNull, shouldNotBeNull, shouldHaveSize\n4. Use MockK: strictMock(), relaxedMock(), every { }, verify { }, slot<T>()\n5. Use TestDataFactory pattern for test data\n6. Cover: Happy path, error handling, edge cases, null/empty inputs\n\nGenerate comprehensive test cases covering all modified code paths."
  }
}
